<http://fairness_ontology.com/In-processing> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://fairness_ontology.com/AILifecycleStep> ;
                                             rdfs:label "In-processing" .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/IndependenceFairnessNotion
<http://fairness_ontology.com/IndependenceFairnessNotion> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                          rdfs:subClassOf <http://fairness_ontology.com/GroupFairnessNotion> ;
                                                          <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/source> "https://doi.org/10.1145/3468507.3468511"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                                          <http://semanticscience.org/resource/hasSynonym> "independence fairness"@en ;
                                                          rdfs:label "Independence Fairness Notion"@en ;
                                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The fairness property satisfied when the predicted outcome variable is independent from protected attributes."@en ;
                                                          <https://purl.org/twc/fmo#probabilistic_definition> "Ŷ ⊥ A"@en .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/IndividualFairnessNotion
<http://fairness_ontology.com/IndividualFairnessNotion> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <http://fairness_ontology.com/OutcomeFairnessNotion> ;
                                                        <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/source> "https://doi.org/10.1145/2090236.2090255"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                                        <http://semanticscience.org/resource/hasSynonym> "individual fairness"@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Individual Fairness Notion"@en ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A family of fairness notions with the common objective to ensure that similar individuals are treated similarly by a model. Some notions in this group may be a relaxed version of &quot;strict&quot; individual fairness (i.e., they may treat similar indivduals differently under certain conditions)."@en .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/InstanceLevelRowIntervention
<http://fairness_ontology.com/InstanceLevelRowIntervention> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                            rdfs:subClassOf <http://fairness_ontology.com/DataResourcesMitigation> ;
                                                            rdfs:label "Feature-level Row Intervention (B)" .


