###  https://purl.org/twc/fmo#bias
<https://purl.org/twc/fmo#bias> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing ;
                                <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/source> "https://www.lexico.com/en/definition/bias"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                rdfs:label "Bias" ;
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Predisposition in favor of or against one thing, person, or group compared with another, usually in a way considered to be unfair."@en .


###  https://purl.org/twc/fmo#fairness_metric
<https://purl.org/twc/fmo#fairness_metric> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf <http://fairness_ontology.com/ScientificArtifact> ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/source> "https://doi.org/10.1145/3468507.3468511"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                           rdfs:label "Fairness Metric"@en ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A measurement of some fairness notion in a machine-learning model or dataset, with regards to some specific cohort(s)."@en .


###  https://purl.org/twc/fmo#fairness_notion
<https://purl.org/twc/fmo#fairness_notion> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf <http://fairness_ontology.com/ScientificArtifact> ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/source> "https://doi.org/10.1145/3468507.3468511"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                           <http://semanticscience.org/resource/hasSynonym> "criterion"@en ,
                                                                                            "fairness"@en ;
                                           rdfs:label "Fairness Notion"@en ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """A conceptual or normative principle that specifies what it means for an AI
system to be fair, i.e., a formal definition of fairness that can be observed as a property of an AI model, in relation to that model's treatment of different cohorts."""@en .


