                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/StatisticalParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/TestFairness> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/itsComplianceIsSupportedWith> <http://fairness_ontology.com/AddNonToxicExamples> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/AdversarialFDP> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/AugmentedAntidoteData> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/BlocklistDocumentRemoval> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/CDA> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/CalibratedReRanking> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ControlOffensiveTokens> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ListReAdjustment> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/LogLikeDocumentRemoval> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/PerceptronForUnawareness> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/REALTOXICITYPROMPTS> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ReSamplingProtectedGroup> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/RegularizationOnANOVA> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/RegularizationOnValueFairness> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/UserItemReRanking> ;
                                      <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000068> <http://fairness_ontology.com/EU_AI_Act> ;
                                      rdfs:comment "Requires that high-risk AI systems be designed and developed with effective human oversight, enabling human operators to understand, monitor and intervene to prevent or minimise harm, including discriminatory outcomes. Notes: Art. 14 binds fairness monitoring to human interventions: define operator-facing fairness signals, thresholds and escalation; enable override/adjustment actions and corrective controls; evidence effectiveness through improvements in the same monitored metrics." .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.15
<http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.15> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/LegalRequirement> ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/TechnicalLegalRequirement> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/isOperationalizedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Calibration> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/ConditionalStatisticalParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/CounterfactualFairness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/DemographicParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualOpportunity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualizedOdds> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/ErrorRateBalance> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/FairnessThroughAwareness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/FalseNegativeErrorRateBalance> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/FalsePositiveErrorRateBalance> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/IndividualFairness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/PredictiveEquality> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/StatisticalParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/TestFairness> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/itsComplianceIsSupportedWith> <http://fairness_ontology.com/AddNonToxicExamples> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/AdvBERT> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/AdvPredictedScore> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/AugmentedAntidoteData> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/BlocklistDocumentRemoval> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/CDA> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/CalibratedReRanking> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ChangeAttentionScores> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ChangeAttentionWeights> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ControlOffensiveTokens> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/DropoutOnAttention> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/InferenceSubnetworks> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ListReAdjustment> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/LogLikeDocumentRemoval> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/OSCAR> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/REALTOXICITYPROMPTS> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ReSamplingProtectedGroup> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/RegularizationOnANOVA> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/RegularizationOnValueFairness> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/UserItemReRanking> ;
                                      <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000068> <http://fairness_ontology.com/EU_AI_Act> ;
                                      rdfs:comment "Requires high-risk AI systems to achieve appropriate levels of accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity, and to maintain these properties throughout the lifecycle. Notes: Art. 15 is mapped to robustness and cybersecurity monitoring where degradations can create group-conditional harms. Fairness indicators are used as robustness evidence (error gaps, calibration/divergence drift, local consistency); mitigations are technical controls activated to restore dependability and evidenced via improvements in the same metrics." .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.16
<http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.16> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/LegalRequirement> ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/ManagementLegalRequirement> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/isOperationalizedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Calibration> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/ConditionalStatisticalParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/CounterfactualFairness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/DemographicParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualOpportunity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualizedOdds> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/ErrorRateBalance> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/FairnessThroughAwareness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/FalseNegativeErrorRateBalance> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/FalsePositiveErrorRateBalance> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/IndividualFairness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/PredictiveEquality> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/StatisticalParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/TestFairness> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/itsComplianceIsSupportedWith> <http://fairness_ontology.com/AddNonToxicExamples> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/AdversarialFDP> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/AugmentedAntidoteData> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/BlocklistDocumentRemoval> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/CDA> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/CalibratedReRanking> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ControlOffensiveTokens> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ListReAdjustment> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/LogLikeDocumentRemoval> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/PerceptronForUnawareness> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/REALTOXICITYPROMPTS> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ReSamplingProtectedGroup> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/RegularizationOnANOVA> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/RegularizationOnValueFairness> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/UserItemReRanking> ;
                                      <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000068> <http://fairness_ontology.com/EU_AI_Act> ;
                                      rdfs:comment "Sets out the obligations of providers of high-risk AI systems, including designing and developing systems in accordance with the requirements and implementing risk management, data governance and monitoring procedures. Notes: Art. 16 is an umbrella provider-duty clause. Mapped notions/metrics form a provider-level evidence portfolio; mapped techniques form the provider control catalogue applied across the lifecycle with documented thresholds, escalation and change management." .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.17
<http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.17> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/LegalRequirement> ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/ManagementLegalRequirement> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/isOperationalizedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Calibration> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/ConditionalStatisticalParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/CounterfactualFairness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/DemographicParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualOpportunity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualizedOdds> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/ErrorRateBalance> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/FairnessThroughAwareness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/FalseNegativeErrorRateBalance> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/FalsePositiveErrorRateBalance> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/IndividualFairness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/PredictiveEquality> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/StatisticalParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/TestFairness> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/itsComplianceIsSupportedWith> <http://fairness_ontology.com/AdversarialFDP> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/AugmentedAntidoteData> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/CDA> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/CalibratedReRanking> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/FairPSL> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ListReAdjustment> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/PerceptronForUnawareness> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ReSamplingProtectedGroup> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/RegularizationOnANOVA> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/RegularizationOnValueFairness> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/UserItemReRanking> ;
                                      <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000068> <http://fairness_ontology.com/EU_AI_Act> ;
                                      rdfs:comment "Requires providers to establish and maintain a quality management system covering design, development, testing, validation, data management and monitoring processes for high-risk AI systems. Notes: Art. 17 operationalises compliance via a QMS: define measurable fairness acceptance criteria (release/regression gates), govern approved mitigation methods, document evidence and limitations, and ensure monitoring plus corrective actions are consistently applied across the lifecycle." .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.2
<http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                              <http://fairness_ontology.com/LegalRequirement> ,
                                              <http://fairness_ontology.com/ManagementLegalRequirement> ;
                                     <http://fairness_ontology.com/isOperationalizedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Calibration> ,
                                                                                        <http://fairness_ontology.com/CounterfactualFairness> ,
                                                                                        <http://fairness_ontology.com/DemographicParity> ,
                                                                                        <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualOpportunity> ,
                                                                                        <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualizedOdds> ,
                                                                                        <http://fairness_ontology.com/StatisticalParity> ,
                                                                                        <http://fairness_ontology.com/TestFairness> ;
                                     <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000068> <http://fairness_ontology.com/EU_AI_Act> ;
                                     rdfs:comment "Defines the subject matter and scope of the Regulation, specifying which AI systems and providers fall under the uniform requirements, including those on fundamental-rights protection and non-discrimination. Notes: Art. 2 is a scope rule: notions/metrics are mapped as applicability anchors (taxonomy for the types of discrimination evidence referenced by downstream obligations), not as performance thresholds required by Art. 2 itself." .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.20
<http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.20> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/LegalRequirement> ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/ManagementLegalRequirement> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/isOperationalizedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Calibration> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/CounterfactualFairness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/DemographicParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualOpportunity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualizedOdds> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/FairnessThroughAwareness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/IndividualFairness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/StatisticalParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/TestFairness> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/itsComplianceIsSupportedWith> <http://fairness_ontology.com/AdversarialFDP> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/AugmentedAntidoteData> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/CDA> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/CalibratedReRanking> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ListReAdjustment> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/PerceptronForUnawareness> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ReSamplingProtectedGroup> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/RegularizationOnANOVA> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/RegularizationOnValueFairness> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/UserItemReRanking> ;
                                      <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000068> <http://fairness_ontology.com/EU_AI_Act> ;
                                      rdfs:comment "Corrective actions and duty of information: when a high-risk AI system is non-compliant or presents a risk, the provider must take corrective actions without undue delay (bring into conformity, withdraw/recall, or disable as appropriate) and promptly inform relevant economic operators and competent actors, providing details of the non-compliance/risk and actions taken. Notes: Art. 20 is a remediation and information-duty clause: fairness notions/metrics serve as operational triggers and regression evidence; mapped techniques are corrective controls applied via change management (update/rollback/withdrawal/disable) with before/after metric verification and notification duties." .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.21
<http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.21> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/LegalRequirement> ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/ManagementLegalRequirement> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/isOperationalizedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Calibration> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/CounterfactualFairness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/DemographicParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualOpportunity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualizedOdds> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/StatisticalParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/TestFairness> ;
                                      <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000068> <http://fairness_ontology.com/EU_AI_Act> ;
                                      rdfs:comment "Requires providers of high-risk AI systems to cooperate with competent authorities and, upon reasoned request, provide necessary information and documentation to demonstrate compliance; where applicable, provide access to automatically generated logs under their control. Notes: Assurance obligation: notions/metrics define the “compliance evidence package” that must be producible, versioned, and interpretable by authorities, including monitoring outputs and (where relevant) log-based evidence." .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.23
<http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.23> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/LegalRequirement> ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/ManagementLegalRequirement> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/isOperationalizedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Calibration> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/CounterfactualFairness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/DemographicParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualOpportunity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualizedOdds> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/StatisticalParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/TestFairness> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/itsComplianceIsSupportedWith> <http://fairness_ontology.com/AdversarialFDP> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/AugmentedAntidoteData> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/CDA> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/CalibratedReRanking> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ListReAdjustment> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/PerceptronForUnawareness> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/ReSamplingProtectedGroup> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/RegularizationOnANOVA> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/RegularizationOnValueFairness> ,
                                                                                                  <http://fairness_ontology.com/UserItemReRanking> ;
                                      <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000068> <http://fairness_ontology.com/EU_AI_Act> ;
                                      rdfs:comment "Sets obligations for importers of high-risk AI systems to verify conformity (incl. required compliance artefacts and instructions), refrain from market placement when non-compliant, ensure storage/transport do not compromise compliance, and cooperate with competent authorities including corrective actions where needed. Notes: Art. 23 acts as a supply-chain compliance gate: notions/metrics define what must be checkable and transferable; mitigation techniques are mapped as documented controls whose configuration and effectiveness evidence must remain aligned with the marketed version and intended context." .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.24
<http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.24> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/LegalRequirement> ,
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/ManagementLegalRequirement> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/isOperationalizedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Calibration> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/CounterfactualFairness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/DemographicParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualOpportunity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/EqualizedOdds> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/FairnessThroughAwareness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/IndividualFairness> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/StatisticalParity> ,
                                                                                         <http://fairness_ontology.com/TestFairness> ;
                                      <http://fairness_ontology.com/itsComplianceIsSupportedWith> <http://fairness_ontology.com/AddNonToxicExamples> ,
