                                   <http://fairness_ontology.com/isProposedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/2020_LU> ;
                                   <http://fairness_ontology.com/scientificArtifactDescription> "Use CDA to mitigate occupation-gender bias, creating matched pairs by flipping gendered (e.g., “he” and “she”) or definitionally gendered (e.g., “king” and “queen”) words, while preserving grammatical and semantic correctness, under the definition that an unbiased model should consider each sentence in a pair equally." .


