                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/hasBeenAppliedTo> <http://fairness_ontology.com/LawAndJustice> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/isProposedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/2020_JUNGa> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/refersTo> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Classification> .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/EquityOfAmortizedAttention
<http://fairness_ontology.com/EquityOfAmortizedAttention> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                   <http://fairness_ontology.com/GroupFairnessNotion> ,
                                                                   <http://fairness_ontology.com/IndependenceFairnessNotion> ,
                                                                   <http://fairness_ontology.com/ObservationalFairnessNotion> ,
                                                                   <http://fairness_ontology.com/OutcomeFairnessNotion> ,
                                                                   <http://fairness_ontology.com/ScientificArtifact> ,
                                                                   <https://purl.org/twc/fmo#fairness_notion> ;
                                                          <http://fairness_ontology.com/isEquivalentTo> <http://fairness_ontology.com/QualityWeightedFairness> ;
                                                          <http://fairness_ontology.com/isMeasuredBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Variance> ;
                                                          <http://fairness_ontology.com/isProposedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/2018_BIEGA> ;
                                                          <http://fairness_ontology.com/scientificArtifactDescription> """A sequence of rankings $\\rho_1, \\dots, \\rho_m$ offers equity of amortized attention if each subject receives cumulative attention proportional to her cumulative relevance, i.e.:

\\[
\\frac{\\sum_{l=1}^{m} a^l_{i_1}}{\\sum_{l=1}^{m} r^l_{i_1}} = 
\\frac{\\sum_{l=1}^{m} a^l_{i_2}}{\\sum_{l=1}^{m} r^l_{i_2}}, 
\\quad \\forall u_{i_1}, u_{i_2}.
\\]""" .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/EquityOfAttention
<http://fairness_ontology.com/EquityOfAttention> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                          <http://fairness_ontology.com/GroupFairnessNotion> ,
                                                          <http://fairness_ontology.com/IndependenceFairnessNotion> ,
                                                          <http://fairness_ontology.com/ObservationalFairnessNotion> ,
                                                          <http://fairness_ontology.com/OutcomeFairnessNotion> ,
                                                          <http://fairness_ontology.com/ScientificArtifact> ,
                                                          <https://purl.org/twc/fmo#fairness_notion> ;
                                                 <http://fairness_ontology.com/isEquivalentTo> <http://fairness_ontology.com/QualityWeightedFairness> ;
                                                 <http://fairness_ontology.com/isMeasuredBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Variance> ;
                                                 <http://fairness_ontology.com/isProposedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/2018_BIEGA> ;
                                                 <http://fairness_ontology.com/scientificArtifactDescription> """A ranking offers equity of  attention if each (ranked) subject receives attention proportional to its relevance. Given: $r^j_i$ the [0..1]-normalized relevance score of subject $u_i$ in  ranking $\\rho_j ,  $a^j_i$ the [0..1]-normalized attention value received by subject $u_i$ in ranking $\\rho_j$, it states: \\[
\\frac{a_{i_1}}{r_{i_1}} = \\frac{a_{i_2}}{r_{i_2}},
\\quad \\forall\\, u_{i_1}, u_{i_2}.
\\]""" .


