###  http://fairness_ontology.com/QualityWeightedFairness
<http://fairness_ontology.com/QualityWeightedFairness> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                <http://fairness_ontology.com/GroupFairnessNotion> ,
                                                                <http://fairness_ontology.com/IndependenceFairnessNotion> ,
                                                                <http://fairness_ontology.com/ObservationalFairnessNotion> ,
                                                                <http://fairness_ontology.com/OutcomeFairnessNotion> ,
                                                                <http://fairness_ontology.com/ScientificArtifact> ,
                                                                <https://purl.org/twc/fmo#fairness_notion> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/isEquivalentTo> <http://fairness_ontology.com/EquityOfAttention> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/isMeasuredBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Variance> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/isProposedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/2021_WU> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/isUsedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/2018_BIEGA> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/scientificArtifactDescription> """A recommendation result is quality weighted fair exposure for providers if each provider in P receives exposure ($e_p$) proportional to the sum of quality scores (i.e., ratings) of items it offers ($I_p$) in the recommendation lists of all customers, i.e., $\\frac{e_{p_1}}{\\sum_{i \\in I_{p_1}} \\sum_{u \\in U} v_{u,i}}= \\frac{e_{p_2}}{ \\sum_{i \\in I_{p_2}} \\sum_{u \\in U} v_{u,i}},
\\quad \\forall\\, p_1, p_2 \\in P .$""" ;
                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "the metric is first used in 2018_BIEGA, but the formailization is due to a later work by 2021_WU" .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/REALTOXICITYPROMPTS
<http://fairness_ontology.com/REALTOXICITYPROMPTS> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/BlackBoxDecisionOnly> ,
                                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/MitigationTechnique> ,
                                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/ModelAccessResourcesMitigation> ,
                                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/OutputRewriting> ,
                                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/ScientificArtifact> ;
                                                   <http://fairness_ontology.com/isProposedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/2020_GEHMAN> ;
                                                   <http://fairness_ontology.com/scientificArtifactDescription> "adaptive pretraining on non-toxic data: increase the likelihood of non-toxic tokens, adding a (non-)toxicity score to the logits over the vocabulary before normalization, ans use word- or ngram-blocking during decoding, prohibiting the use of tokens from an offensive word list" .


