###  http://fairness_ontology.com/RelativeLInfiniteMetric
<http://fairness_ontology.com/RelativeLInfiniteMetric> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                <http://fairness_ontology.com/DistanceBasedFairnessMetric> ,
                                                                <http://fairness_ontology.com/ScientificArtifact> ,
                                                                <https://purl.org/twc/fmo#fairness_metric> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/extends> <http://fairness_ontology.com/FairnessThroughAwareness> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/hasBeenAppliedTo> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Education> ,
                                                                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/Healthcare> ,
                                                                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/LawAndJustice> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/isProposedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/2012_DWORK> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/isUsedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/2018_YONA> ,
                                                                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/2019_LAHOTI> ,
                                                                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/2020_YUROCHKIN> ,
                                                                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/2025_GAO> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/measures> <http://fairness_ontology.com/FairnessThroughAwareness> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/refersTo> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Classification> ;
                                                       <http://fairness_ontology.com/scientificArtifactDescription> "Given P and Q, probability measures on a finite domain A, total variation norm suggests to compute the distance between the distributions as: $D_{\\infty}(P, Q) = \\sup_{a \\in A} \\log \\!\\left( \\max \\left\\{ \\frac{P(a)}{Q(a)}, \\frac{Q(a)}{P(a)} \\right\\} \\right) .$" ;
                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "It is the second poposed metric connected to the notion of Fairness through awareness" .


