###  http://fairness_ontology.com/UniformFairness
<http://fairness_ontology.com/UniformFairness> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                        <http://fairness_ontology.com/GroupFairnessNotion> ,
                                                        <http://fairness_ontology.com/IndependenceFairnessNotion> ,
                                                        <http://fairness_ontology.com/ObservationalFairnessNotion> ,
                                                        <http://fairness_ontology.com/OutcomeFairnessNotion> ,
                                                        <http://fairness_ontology.com/ScientificArtifact> ,
                                                        <https://purl.org/twc/fmo#fairness_notion> ;
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/isMeasuredBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/Variance> ;
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/isProposedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/2021_WU> ;
                                               <http://fairness_ontology.com/scientificArtifactDescription> """A recommendation result has  the property of uniform fair exposure for providers if each provider receives exposure ($e_p$) proportional to the number of items it offers ($I_p$), i.e., $\\frac{e_{p_1}}{\\lvert I_{p_1} \\rvert} = \\frac{e_{p_2}}{\\lvert I_{p_2} \\rvert},
\\quad \\forall\\, p_1, p_2 \\in P $, where P is the set of providers. Note that providers can be seen as groups of items. Hence, this is a group fairness notion.""" .


