###  http://fairness_ontology.com/rND
<http://fairness_ontology.com/rND> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/GranularityMetric> ,
                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/ItemFocusedMetric> ,
                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/OptimizationObjectMetric> ,
                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/RecommendationSystemMetric> ,
                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/ScientificArtifact> ,
                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/SingleGranularityMetric> ,
                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/SubjectMetric> ,
                                            <http://fairness_ontology.com/TreatmentFocusedMetric> ,
                                            <https://purl.org/twc/fmo#fairness_metric> ;
                                   <http://fairness_ontology.com/isProposedBy> <http://fairness_ontology.com/2017_YANG> ;
                                   <http://fairness_ontology.com/measures> <http://fairness_ontology.com/StatisticalParity> ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "(*)Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain is a ranking metric used to evaluate recommendation systems by measuring the quality of the ranked list of recommended items. It assesses a system's ability to place the most relevant items at the top of the list, with higher scores indicating a better ranking. NDCG is calculated by dividing the Discounted Cumulative Gain (DCG) of the actual recommendation list by the DCG of an ideal list, resulting in a score between 0 and 1." .


