<http://fairness_ontology.com/Disparagement> rdfs:label "disparagement"@en ;
                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Disparagement is not merely bias in representation but bias in expression, it is the linguistic realization of stereotype."@en .


<http://fairness_ontology.com/Prejudice> rdfs:label "prejudice"@en ;
                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Prejudice is a latent human or cultural construct and represents historical predispositions to discrimination."@en .


<http://fairness_ontology.com/Stereotype> rdfs:label "stereotype"@en ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A simplified and generalized representation of a group (e.g., “women are nurses,” “men are engineers”) that operationalizes discrimination in communication, media, or data."@en .


<http://fairness_ontology.com/hasAntonym> rdfs:comment "Relates a concept to its antonym, given as a string or URI."@en ;
                                          rdfs:label "has antonym"@en .


